# SmolServe v1.1.0

Currently, I'm working on adding support for the Nex Protocol{a} to Rogallo{b}. Having Port1900{c} as the client library, and having done the bulk of the work in Rogallo{d}, I needed things in place to be able to add some `nex://`-related documentation too -- which is where SmolServe{e} comes in.

=> https://blog.davep.org/tag/nex-protocol/ {a} Nex Protocol
=> https://rogallo.davep.dev/ {b} Rogallo
=> https://blog.davep.org/2026/08/14/port1900-an-async-python-client-library-for-the-nex-protocol.html {c} Port1900
=> https://github.com/davep/rogallo/pull/345 {d} done the bulk of the work in Rogallo
=> https://smolserve.davep.dev/ {e} SmolServe

So I've dropped v1.1.0{a} on PyPI{b}, which adds support for running up a simple just-good-enough Nex server (although, to be fair, Nex is *so* simple this is probably a fully capable one just by the very nature of how trivial the protocol is).

=> https://smolserve.davep.dev/changelog/#v110 {a} v1.1.0
=> https://blog.davep.org/tag/pypi/ {b} PyPI

Now to get back to polishing that Rogallo PR...

